message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
title: "wildfire-marl: Hierarchical Multi-Agent Reinforcement Learning for Wildfire Suppression on Validated Fire Physics"
authors:
  - family-names: Akarma
    given-names: Ali
version: 2.0.0a0
date-released: "2026-07-19"
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/aliakarma/wildfire-rl"
keywords:
  - multi-agent-reinforcement-learning
  - wildfire
  - cell2fire
  - mappo
  - hierarchical-reinforcement-learning
  - transfer-learning
  - geospatial
  - remote-sensing
  - domain-generalization
  - benchmark
abstract: >
  wildfire-marl is a reproducible benchmark and method for multi-agent wildfire suppression on
  validated fire physics. Firefighting agents defend critical infrastructure under Cell2Fire, a
  peer-reviewed C++ simulator of the Canadian Forest Fire Behaviour Prediction system, on real
  7-channel geospatial landscapes (ERA5 weather, SRTM terrain, MODIS NDVI fuel, FIRMS ignitions)
  for two dissimilar regimes: Saudi Arabia's Eastern Province and Northern California. The
  proposed hierarchical policy, HierComm, is compared against information-matched heuristics and
  flat multi-agent RL over five training seeds with disjoint train/eval ignition streams,
  bootstrap confidence intervals, effect sizes, single-factor ablations, and a symmetric
  cross-regional transfer protocol. All reported artifacts are SHA-256 fingerprinted and frozen.
